    "details": "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1282 reports:\n\n> Expat before 2.8.5 fails to validate that a high surrogate in UTF-16\n> input is followed by a low surrogate, allowing malformed UTF-16\n> sequences to be accepted. Attackers can supply UTF-16 encoded XML\n> containing lone high surrogates that consume the following code unit,\n> causing Expat to pass unpaired surrogates to applications built with\n> XML_UNICODE and to silently replace input characters in other builds.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0492",
